# ── Audience analytics (dummy figures) ──
# Every value below is a FAKE number shown in the "Audience analytics" card.
# Each figure drifts up AND down within ±JITTER of its BASE, so it looks live
# without ballooning. There are two ways to set them (runtime wins):
#
#   • ON THE SERVER (runtime, no rebuild) — name this file `.env` next to
#     docker-compose.yml. The container reads it on start and regenerates
#     /analytics-config.js, so editing a value + `docker compose up -d` updates
#     the numbers live. This is the normal way to bump them.
#
#   • IN THE REPO (build-time fallback) — `.env.production` is baked into the
#     image at build. Used for SSR / first paint and whenever no runtime value
#     is set. Keep it as a sane default.
#
#   *_BASE   = the number the figure hovers around. Bump as the real numbers grow.
#   *_JITTER = drift amplitude (build-time only). Small = subtle; 0 = frozen.

# IG + TikTok · Followers
NEXT_PUBLIC_FOLLOWERS_BASE=5000
NEXT_PUBLIC_FOLLOWERS_JITTER=15

# IG + TikTok · Views
NEXT_PUBLIC_VIEWS_BASE=1000000
NEXT_PUBLIC_VIEWS_JITTER=600

# Bola Aja YT · Subscribers
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUBS_BASE=20000
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUBS_JITTER=20

# Bola Aja YT · Views
NEXT_PUBLIC_YT_VIEWS_BASE=36000000
NEXT_PUBLIC_YT_VIEWS_JITTER=4000

# "+X today" views ticker seed (drifts up slowly during a session)
NEXT_PUBLIC_VIEWS_TODAY_BASE=14382
